{"text":"The defect has been located, fixed, and verified:\n\n**Defect:** In `src/paginate.js`, the `pageBounds` function computed the end offset as `start + pageSize - 1`, which is inclusive. This caused an off-by-one error — for example, with page 2 (0-indexed), page size 10, and total 23 records, it returned `{ start: 20, end: 22 }` instead of the correct exclusive-boundary result `{ start: 20, end: 23 }`.\n\n**Fix:** Changed `Math.min(start + pageSize - 1, total)` to `Math.min(start + pageSize, total)`, making the end offset exclusive to match the test expectations and standard half-open interval semantics `[start, end)`. The public API (`pageBounds(page, pageSize, total)`) was not changed.\n\n**Verification:** Both tests pass:\n- ✔ uses an exclusive end offset on a partial final page\n- ✔ does not include a phantom record on a complete page","toolCalls":[],"finishReason":"stop"}